  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Read the two paths",
      "items": [
        "Top: Postgres \u2192 dlt \u2192 bronze \u2192 dbt \u2192 curated ClickHouse. Dagster owns orchestration.",
        "Middle: select the analytics agent \u2192 discover semantics \u2192 query curated data \u2192 answer or chart. The companion workflow expands this path."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Privacy and warehouse access",
      "items": [
        "Extraction removes document/message bodies, run inputs, store values and checkpoint state before loading. Some identifiers and display names remain.",
        "The analytics_agent database user has SELECT on staging and marts only: 30 seconds and 10,000 result rows, with server-enforced maxima."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Meaning and consumers",
      "items": [
        "dbt owns tables and column descriptions; Cube supplies metric definitions through /cubejs-api/v1/meta. The agent queries ClickHouse directly.",
        "Cube also has a configured ClickHouse query backend and optional SQL Lab connection; neither is the seeded dashboard or agent SQL path."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Interpretation and scope",
      "items": [
        "The schedule is hourly, not real-time. Message first_seen_at records capture time; historical backfill shares the first capture window.",
        "Cost is a list-price estimate; interrupted means approval pause. This is repository architecture, not a live health check.",
        "Source snapshot: 30cc0bc. Existing local changes: skills-lock.json and untracked Archify/Archify Review skills; cited runtime files are committed."
      ]
    }
  ]
